+# Fälligkeitsdatum Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Optional `dueDate` on todos, a server-computed `overdue` flag, an `?overdue=` filter, and a list page that shows the date, marks overdue todos and can show only overdue ones.
+
+**Architecture:** The store validates and stores `dueDate`, and decorates every returned todo with `overdue` computed from an injectable clock (UTC date). The app parses `?overdue=` and passes it to `store.list`. The page renders from the API's fields only.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Node 24, `node:http`, `node:test`, plain HTML/JS. No dependencies.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-23-faelligkeitsdatum-design.md`
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Zero dependencies, Node builtins only.
+- `dueDate` is `YYYY-MM-DD` or `null`; "heute" = current date in UTC.
+- `overdue = !done && dueDate !== null && dueDate < today`.
+- Invalid input → `ValidationError` (HTTP 400).
+- New UI elements carry `data-testid`: `todo-due-date`, `todo-overdue`, `overdue-filter`.
+- UI copy, exact: marker `überfällig`, checkbox label `nur überfällige`; date shown as `TT.MM.JJJJ`.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- Nonexistent calendar days (`2026-02-30`, `2027-02-29`) must be 400; leap day `2028-02-29` valid. → Task 1 test `validates dueDate`.
+- Date-like strings with extra parts (`2026-10-23T10:00`, `2026-1-5`, `""`) must be 400. → Task 1 test `validates dueDate`.
+- UTC boundary: at `2026-10-23T23:30:00Z` today is `2026-10-23` (not Berlin's 24th). → Task 1 test `uses the UTC date for today`.
+- Marking an overdue todo done clears `overdue` immediately. → Task 1 test `computes overdue`.
+- `?overdue=` with empty or other value (`yes`, `1`) must be 400, not silently unfiltered. → Task 2 test `rejects invalid overdue filter`.
+
+---
+
+### Task 1: Store — dueDate, overdue, clock, list filter
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `src/store.mjs`
+- Test: `test/store.test.mjs` (create)
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Produces: `createStore({ now = () => new Date() } = {})`. Every method that returns a todo returns a fresh object `{ id, title, done, dueDate, overdue }` (stored record stays `{ id, title, done, dueDate }`; `overdue` computed per call). `list({ overdue } = {})` — `overdue` is `undefined` (all), `true` or `false` (filter). `add({ title, dueDate })` — `dueDate` optional, defaults to `null`. `update(id, patch)` accepts `dueDate` (`string | null`). Unknown fields, including `overdue`, are ignored.
